Here’s a **clean, real-world way** to integrate any **Admin/Agent dashboard HTML template** into **Laravel Blade** (so it’s modular: header/sidebar/footer, one CSS/JS load, and pages extend the layout). This fits your project style (no Vite needed, use `public/assets/...`).

---

## 1) Put Template Assets in `public/`

Create this structure:

```
public/
  assets/
    css/
      dashboard.css
      auth.css
    js/
      dashboard.js
    img/
      logo.png
```

✅ Put your template files exactly here (CSS/JS/images).

---

## 2) Create Main Layout (Admin / Agent can share)

Create: `resources/views/layouts/dashboard.blade.php`

```blade
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <title>{{ $title ?? 'Dashboard' }}</title>

  {{-- Template CSS --}}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('assets/css/dashboard.css') }}">

  @stack('styles')
</head>
<body>

  <div class="app">

    {{-- Sidebar --}}
    @include('partials.sidebar')

    <div class="main">

      {{-- Topbar/Header --}}
      @include('partials.header', ['pageTitle' => $pageTitle ?? 'Dashboard'])

      {{-- Page Content --}}
      <main class="content">
        @yield('content')
      </main>

      {{-- Footer (optional) --}}
      @includeWhen(View::exists('partials.footer'), 'partials.footer')

    </div>
  </div>

  {{-- Template JS --}}
  <script src="{{ asset('assets/js/dashboard.js') }}"></script>
  @stack('scripts')
</body>
</html>
```

